(7491216, 1189680, 115814, '<td valign="top">Hi Leo,<br/> <br/>I note you''re a new member, here and your first entry was a great success, then was disqualified. Although this one didn''t score as well as the first one, I think it has lots of potential. As in your first entry, you''ve made effective choices for slower shutter speed creating an attractive blur in the moving water. For this image, I think the "interesting sky" contributes to overall flat lighting and has the effect of creating a overall low-contrast image. <br/> <br/>I don''t know what your processing workflow is, but if this is a raw image, you should have some leverage with shadow and highlight adjustment that might provide a wider range of tonal contrast. <br/> <br/>Glad to see you joining our community. Looking forward to seeing more!<br/> <br/>[Edited for minor typo]<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-01-08 14:25:40.</i></td>', 'Hi Leo, I note you''re a new member, here and your first entry was a great success, then was disqualified. Although this one didn''t score as well as the first one, I think it has lots of potential. As in your first entry, you''ve made effective choices for slower shutter speed creating an attractive blur in the moving water. For this image, I think the "interesting sky" contributes to overall flat lighting and has the effect of creating a overall low-contrast image.  I don''t know what your processing workflow is, but if this is a raw image, you should have some leverage with shadow and highlight adjustment that might provide a wider range of tonal contrast.  Glad to see you joining our community. Looking forward to seeing more! [Edited for minor typo]', '2017-01-08 14:24:43.000000', '2017-01-08 14:25:40.000000', 0),
